    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01HDHJB4TXSB2M0FZWSVRCJSCM\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to identify push notification subscribers who are highly engaged with your marketing. Once you identify these subscribers in a segment, send campaigns to this group to ensure you only contact people who want to hear from you. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HDHJB4TXJ1ECXC14J01MTFVN\">Before you begin </h2>\n<p>Before creating a segment of engaged push subscribers: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Set up <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360023213971\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">iOS</a> and <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/14750928993307\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Android</a> push notifications in Klaviyo </li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360006653972\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Send your first push campaign</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/15038587235995\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Set up a push welcome flow</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>These steps ensure you have engagement data in your account. Without engagement data, your segment of engaged push subscribers will be empty. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HDHJB4TX3G2SSE91NA4GKXQF\">Create an engaged push subscriber segment</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Audience &gt; Lists &amp; segments</strong> in Klaviyo. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create New</strong>. </li>\n<li>Choose <strong>Create s</strong><strong>egment</strong>. </li>\n<li>Create a segment with the following definition:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>If someone can or cannot receive marketing &gt; can receive &gt; mobile push marketing<br>AND</li>\n<li>What someone has done &gt; Opened push is at least X in the last 30 days</li>\n</ul>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HDHJB4TXQ1X9B67PM995YQZ4\">Create advanced engaged push subscriber segments with custom metrics</h2>\n<p>Klaviyo provides the following built-in push metrics: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Received push</li>\n<li>Opened push</li>\n<li>Bounced push </li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your developer team can build additional push metrics. Some examples of metrics you can custom-build are: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Active on app </li>\n<li>Logged in to app </li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you have built custom engagement metrics like these, consider using them in your engaged segment. Add additional custom metrics to your segment using an OR connector, like: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>If someone can or cannot receive marketing &gt; can receive &gt; mobile push marketing<br>AND</li>\n<li>What someone has done &gt; Opened push is at least X in the last 30 days<br>OR</li>\n<li>What someone has done &gt; Active on app &gt; at least X in the last 30 days</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HDHJB4TX7PDT0QB1JVY343K8\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/14781686592283\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Understanding push notification consent</a></li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/13769219837083\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">How to increase push notifications opens</a> </li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
